  SECTION 4 — PROTECTED INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

The following elements of the Software are explicitly protected and may NOT
be reproduced, adapted, or used as the basis for any other work without
written permission, even for non-commercial purposes:

  4.1 SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE & PIPELINE DESIGN
      • The five-stage intelligence pipeline: Ingestion → Relevance Filtering
        → Dual-Stage Classification → Storage → Reporting, implemented
        across sources.py, pipeline.py, taxonomy.py, deepseek_client.py,
        reporter.py, and scheduler.py (~4,600 lines total);
      • The APScheduler AsyncIOScheduler job orchestration with five
        coordinated jobs: ingest_job (interval, configurable minutes),
        stock_job (30 min), daily_report_job (cron 08:00), weekly_report_job
        (Sun 08:05), monthly_report_job (month-end 08:10), all keyed to
        Asia/Taipei timezone with coalescing and max_instances=1 guard;
      • The SourceDefinition dataclass schema {name, source_type, url,
        params, macro_hint, tech_hint, skip_page_preview} and the 25
        pre-configured source registry spanning Google News RSS (4 targeted
        queries), arXiv API, Crossref REST API (7 journals), IEEE Xplore RSS
        (4 TOC feeds), Nature RSS (3), and ScienceDirect RSS (3).

  4.2 GaN-SPECIFIC RELEVANCE FILTERING ALGORITHM
      • The _is_gan_relevant_article() function in pipeline.py implementing
        a dual-criteria gate:
        — Inclusion: exact match "gallium nitride" or "氮化镓" (auto-accept),
          OR word-boundary \bGaN\b with co-occurrence of any GAN_SEMICONDUCTOR_HINTS
          {"semiconductor", "power electronics", "hemt", "gan fet", "transistor",
          "charger", "inverter", "mmwave", "wafer", "epitaxy"};
        — Exclusion: automatic rejection if AI/ML tokens detected
          {"generative adversarial", "diffusion", "large language model",
          "machine learning", "image generation"};
      • This algorithm is the proprietary gate that distinguishes GaN power
        semiconductor content from unrelated GAN homograph noise (generative
        adversarial networks) — its specific token sets and logic are
        original intellectual property.

  4.3 DUAL-STAGE CLASSIFICATION SYSTEM
      • Stage 1 — Deterministic Rule Engine (taxonomy.py):
        classify_text(title, summary) returning (macro, tech, tags[])
        via hardcoded _MACRO_RULES and _TECH_RULES keyword lookup tables
        and _TAG_KEYWORDS list, fully offline with zero external API calls.
        Three macro categories: "academic", "industry", "stock".
        Six base tech categories: "low_power", "high_power",
        "high_frequency", "materials", "packaging", "other";
      • Stage 2 — LLM Refinement (deepseek_client.py):
        DeepSeekClient.analyze_article() posting to DeepSeek Chat API
        (model: deepseek-chat, temperature: 0.2, JSON mode) with a
        structured prompt encoding {title, summary, hints, macro_choices,
        tech_choices, task} — the task instruction mandates output of
        macro_category, tech_category, sentiment_score (range -1 to 1),
        impact_score (range 0 to 100), and analysis_text (≤120 words,
        Chinese) in strict JSON format;
      • The AnalysisResult dataclass {macro_category, tech_category,
        sentiment_score, impact_score, analysis_text} and the tenacity
        retry decorator (3 attempts, exponential backoff) with graceful
        fallback to Stage 1 results on failure.

  4.4 CATEGORY HIERARCHY & RESOLUTION LOGIC
      • The CategoryField hierarchical tree model in category_registry.py
        with macro roots (academic/industry/stock) as parents and
        tech categories (industry_low_power, academic_high_frequency, etc.)
        as children, stored in SQLite with composite unique index on
        (group_type, key);
      • The _resolve_tech_choice() smart mapping algorithm:
        — Direct match → return as-is;
        — Prefix reconstruction: "high_power" + macro "industry"
          → "industry_high_power";
        — Fallback chain: "{macro}_other" → "industry_other"
          → "academic_other" → first sorted valid key;
      • The _normalize_article_tech_categories() cascade function that
        reassigns all articles to active categories upon category deletion,
        and the ensure_seed_categories() idempotent seeder.

  4.5 SOURCE VERIFICATION & COMPANY WHITELIST SYSTEM
      • The verify_source_url() algorithm in source_registry.py
        performing three-stage validation: URL format check →
        domain trust check against 49 hardcoded STATIC_TRUSTED_DOMAIN_SUFFIXES
        (including news.google.com, arxiv.org, ieee.org, ieeexplore.ieee.org,
        nature.com, wolfspeed.com, navitassemi.com, vis.com.tw, etc.)
        plus runtime whitelist → HTTP reachability test (15s timeout);
      • The sync_company_whitelist_sources() auto-generation function that
        constructs targeted Google News RSS queries for whitelisted company
        domains using the pattern:
        site:{domain} ("gallium nitride" OR ("GaN" semiconductor))
        -generative -adversarial when:14d
        and idempotently creates/activates/deactivates corresponding source
        entries in the database.

  4.6 MULTI-LEVEL CHINESE REPORTING SYSTEM
      • Three distinct DeepSeek prompt templates for Chinese language
        industry analysis:
        — Daily (100–150 words): 1–3 key dynamics + industry significance;
        — Weekly (200–280 words): tech/industry/market dynamics + trends;
        — Monthly (350–450 words): four-section structured analysis
          (① monthly summary ② vs-prior-month comparison ③ key event
          commentary ④ forward-looking signals);
      • The HTML email rendering pipeline in reporter.py with inline CSS
        and dynamic section composition (AI summary block, macro/tech
        distribution stat-chips, article lists by macro category, monthly
        trend delta tables with up/down indicators), dual transport
        abstraction (Resend API primary, Gmail SMTP fallback);
      • All report sends logged in the ReportLog table with report_type,
        recipient, subject, status, and error_message for audit trails.

  4.7 DATA SCHEMA & STORAGE DESIGN
      • The Article ORM model composite index
        idx_articles_macro_tech_pub (macro_category, tech_category,
        published_at) enabling efficient category-filtered time-range
        queries across the full article corpus;
      • The page preview extraction algorithm in fetch_article_page_preview()
        using BeautifulSoup with meta-tag priority ordering
        (og:description → name=description → twitter:description) and
        structural fallback to <article>/<main>/<body> paragraph content,
        with Google News redirect detection and 6-second timeout.

